## User question:
"How to configure Nokia routers to automatically add a link-bandwidth extended community to unlabeled unicast IPv4 routes received from directly connected EBGP peers?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia routers to automatically add a link-bandwidth extended community to unlabeled unicast IPv4 routes received from directly connected EBGP peers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        type external
        link-bandwidth
            add-to-received-ebgp ipv4
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name. This configuration will apply to all EBGP neighbors in the specified group.
