## Proposed answer:
To configure BGP to propagate routes that are not currently selected as the best path in the routing table, you need to enable BGP Add-Paths functionality. Here are the relevant CLI commands:

For VPN-IPv4 routes:
```
configure router bgp add-paths
    vpn-ipv4 send 3
exit
```

For IPv4 routes:
```
configure router bgp add-paths
    ipv4 send 3
exit
```

These commands configure BGP to advertise up to 3 alternative paths (you can adjust the number as needed) for each prefix to your BGP peers, including non-best paths. The exact number depends on your network requirements and how many alternate paths you want to propagate.

Note that both peers must support the Add-Paths capability for this to work effectively. You may need to configure this at the group or neighbor level if you only want to enable it for specific peers.
