Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure your Nokia router to advertise VPN IPv4 routes over IPv6 transport with an IPv6 address as the BGP next hop, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    family vpn-ipv4 ipv6
    group <group-name>
        family vpn-ipv4
        neighbor <ipv6-neighbor-address>
            local-address <local-ipv6-address>
            family vpn-ipv4
            no shutdown
```

Replace `<group-name>`, `<ipv6-neighbor-address>`, and `<local-ipv6-address>` with your specific values. This configuration:
1. Enables VPN-IPv4 and IPv6 address families at the global BGP level
2. Configures the BGP group to support VPN-IPv4 routes
3. Sets up the IPv6 neighbor with a local IPv6 address
4. Ensures VPN-IPv4 routes will be exchanged with the specified IPv6 next hop
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
How to configure Nokia router BGP to allow VPN IPv4 routes to be advertised over IPv6 transport with an IPv6 address as the BGP next hop?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure your Nokia router to advertise VPN IPv4 routes over IPv6 transport with an IPv6 address as the BGP next hop, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    family vpn-ipv4 ipv6
    group <group-name>
        family vpn-ipv4
        neighbor <ipv6-neighbor-address>
            local-address <local-ipv6-address>
            family vpn-ipv4
            no shutdown
```

Replace `<group-name>`, `<ipv6-neighbor-address>`, and `<local-ipv6-address>` with your specific values. This configuration:
1. Enables VPN-IPv4 and IPv6 address families at the global BGP level
2. Configures the BGP group to support VPN-IPv4 routes
3. Sets up the IPv6 neighbor with a local IPv6 address
4. Ensures VPN-IPv4 routes will be exchanged with the specified IPv6 next hop
