To enable the advertisement of active /32 LDP FEC prefixes with RFC 3107 labels to a BGP peer on a Nokia router, regardless of existing BGP paths for the same prefix, use the following configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        family label-ipv4
        neighbor <peer-ip-address>
            family label-ipv4
            add-paths
                label-ipv4 send 16
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<peer-ip-address>` with the IP address of your BGP peer. This configuration:
1. Enables the label-IPv4 address family
2. Configures add-paths capability for label-IPv4
3. Sets the maximum number of paths (16) to advertise for each prefix

The `label-ipv4 send 16` command ensures all active LDP FEC /32 prefixes will be advertised to the peer, even if multiple paths exist for the same prefix.
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
How to enable the advertisement of active /32 LDP FEC prefixes with RFC 3107 labels to a BGP peer on a Nokia router, regardless of existing BGP paths for the same prefix?
---
## Proposed answer:
To enable the advertisement of active /32 LDP FEC prefixes with RFC 3107 labels to a BGP peer on a Nokia router, regardless of existing BGP paths for the same prefix, use the following configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        family label-ipv4
        neighbor <peer-ip-address>
            family label-ipv4
            add-paths
                label-ipv4 send 16
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<peer-ip-address>` with the IP address of your BGP peer. This configuration:
1. Enables the label-IPv4 address family
2. Configures add-paths capability for label-IPv4
3. Sets the maximum number of paths (16) to advertise for each prefix

The `label-ipv4 send 16` command ensures all active LDP FEC /32 prefixes will be advertised to the peer, even if multiple paths exist for the same prefix.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
advertise-ldp-prefix
no advertise-ldp-prefix
FuncDef:
This command, when configured for a session that supports the IPv4 labeled-unicast address family, allows (subject to BGP export policies) active /32 LDP FEC prefixes to be advertised to the BGP peer with an RFC 3107 label, even though there may be BGP paths for the same prefix.
ParaDef:
No ParaDef found
