Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure BGP on a Nokia router to aggregate bandwidth values from link-bandwidth extended communities for IPv4 routes received from EBGP peers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    multipath 8 ebgp 8
    group <group-name>
        type external
        link-bandwidth
            accept-from-ebgp ipv4
        exit
        neighbor <neighbor-ip>
            peer-as <peer-as-number>
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>`, `<neighbor-ip>`, and `<peer-as-number>` with your specific values. This configuration:
1. Enables BGP multipath with up to 8 paths for both general and EBGP cases
2. Creates an external BGP group
3. Configures the group to accept link-bandwidth extended communities for IPv4 routes from EBGP peers

The router will now consider the bandwidth values from these communities when making multipath decisions for IPv4 routes.
------------
