To configure a Nokia router to set the BGP aggregator path attribute router ID to zero when aggregating routes, use the following CLI command:

```
configure router bgp aggregate-zero-router-id
```

This command ensures that the router ID in the AGGREGATOR attribute is set to zero during route aggregation.
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router to set the BGP aggregator path attribute router ID to zero when aggregating routes?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to set the BGP aggregator path attribute router ID to zero when aggregating routes, use the following CLI command:

```
configure router bgp aggregate-zero-router-id
```

This command ensures that the router ID in the AGGREGATOR attribute is set to zero during route aggregation.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
aggregator-id-zero
no aggregator-id-zero
FuncDef:
This command sets the router ID in the BGP aggregator path attribute to zero when BGP aggregates routes. This prevents different routers within an AS from creating aggregate routes that contain different AS paths.
ParaDef:
No ParaDef found
