Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To enable BGP path selection based on end-to-end IGP metrics for routes in Nokia routers, you need to configure the `ignore-nh-metric` command under the BGP best-path-selection context. This tells BGP to consider the IGP metric when selecting paths rather than ignoring it.

Here are the CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        ignore-nh-metric
    exit
exit
```

This configuration ensures BGP will use the IGP cost to reach the next-hop as part of its path selection criteria.
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
How to enable BGP path selection based on end-to-end IGP metrics for routes in Nokia routers?
---
## Proposed answer:
To enable BGP path selection based on end-to-end IGP metrics for routes in Nokia routers, you need to configure the `ignore-nh-metric` command under the BGP best-path-selection context. This tells BGP to consider the IGP metric when selecting paths rather than ignoring it.

Here are the CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        ignore-nh-metric
    exit
exit
```

This configuration ensures BGP will use the IGP cost to reach the next-hop as part of its path selection criteria.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
aigp
no aigp
FuncDef:
This command enables or disables Accumulated IGP (AIGP) path attribute support with one or more BGP peers. BGP path selection among routes with an associated AIGP metric is based on the end-to-end IGP metrics of the different BGP paths, even when these BGP paths span more than one AS and IGP instance.
ParaDef:
No ParaDef found
