## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router to permit BGP next-hop resolution for labeled IPv4 routes using static routes, excluding default static routes?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to permit BGP next-hop resolution for labeled IPv4 routes using static routes (excluding default static routes), use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        next-hop-resolution
            labeled-routes
                transport-tunnel
                    family label-ipv4
                        resolution-filter
                            static
                                no default
                            exit
                        exit
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enters the BGP next-hop resolution context for labeled routes
2. Configures transport tunnel settings for label-ipv4 family
3. Enables static route resolution while explicitly excluding default static route
