You are an expert assistant in configuring network devices. Based on the user's request and the retrieved content from the router configuration manual below, generate appropriate CLI configuration commands.

---

User Request:  
"How to configure a Nokia router to tie the BGP session state with the underlying BFD session at the neighbor level?"

Retrieved Reference Content (from the configuration manual):  
{
    "PageTitle": "remove-private",
    "FuncDef": "This command allows private AS numbers to be removed from the AS path before advertising them to BGP peers.",
    "CLIs": [
        "remove-private [ limited ] [ skip-peer-as ]",
        "no remove-private"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp",
        "config>router>bgp>group",
        "config>router>bgp>group>neighbor"
    ],
    "ParaDef": [
        {
            "Parameters": "limited",
            "Info": "This optional keyword removes private ASNs up to the first public ASN encountered. It then stops removing private ASNs."
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "skip-peer-as",
            "Info": "This optional keyword causes this command to not remove a private ASN from the AS-Path if that ASN is the same as the BGP peer AS number."
        }
    ],
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no remove-private"
}
{
