To enable BGP routing protocol on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        no shutdown
```

This will create the BGP protocol instance and enable it administratively. You may also want to configure additional BGP parameters such as the router ID, autonomous system number, and peer groups depending on your specific requirements. For example:

```
configure router
    router-id 192.0.2.1
    bgp
        router-id 192.0.2.1
        group "EBGP_PEERS"
            type external
            peer-as 64500
            neighbor 203.0.113.1
                peer-as 64501
            exit
        exit
        no shutdown
```
