To enable BGP tunneling for next-hop resolution of labeled IPv4 routes on a Nokia router, use the following configuration:

```
configure router
    bgp
        next-hop-resolution
            labeled-routes
                transport-tunnel
                    family label-ipv4
                        resolution-filter
                            bgp
                        exit
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enters the BGP context under router configuration
2. Configures next-hop resolution for labeled routes
3. Specifies the label-ipv4 address family
4. Enables BGP tunneling as the resolution method for next-hop resolution of labeled IPv4 routes

Optionally, you may also want to configure:
- `allow-static` under `config>router>bgp>next-hop-res>labeled-routes` if you need to resolve BGP next-hops using static routes
- `backup-path label-ipv4` under `config>router>bgp` for fast reroute capabilities
- `ibgp-multipath` under `config>router>bgp` for load balancing if multiple paths exist
