To configure Nokia routers to prefer BGP routes with a Valid origin validation state over those with a Not-Found state during best path selection, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        compare-origin-validation-state
        origin-invalid-unusable
    exit
exit
```

These commands will:
1. Enable comparison of origin validation states (`compare-origin-validation-state`)
2. Mark routes with Invalid states as unusable (`origin-invalid-unusable`)

The result will be that Valid routes are preferred over Not-Found routes, and Not-Found routes are preferred over Invalid routes in the BGP best path selection process.
