Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To set the BGP Connect Retry timer to 90 seconds on a Nokia router, use the following CLI command:

```
configure router bgp connect-retry 90
``` 

This command can also be applied at the group or neighbor level if needed:

For a specific BGP group:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> connect-retry 90
```

For a specific BGP neighbor:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> connect-retry 90
```
