## User question:
How to configure Nokia router's BGP group to treat received EVPN routes without encapsulation extended community as VXLAN by default?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router's BGP group to treat received EVPN routes without encapsulation extended community as VXLAN by default, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        family evpn
        vpn-apply-import
        vpn-apply-export
exit
```

This configuration ensures that:
1. The BGP group supports the EVPN address family
2. Base instance BGP import policies are applied to EVPN routes
3. Base instance BGP export policies are applied to EVPN routes

The combination of these commands will make the router process EVPN routes according to your default VXLAN treatment when no encapsulation extended community is present.
