## Proposed answer:
To originate a default BGP route (0.0.0.0/0) towards specific peers in a Nokia router's BGP configuration, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        family ipv4
        neighbor <peer-ip-address>
            default-originate
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<peer-ip-address>` with the IP address of the specific peer. The `default-originate` command under the neighbor context will advertise the default route to that peer.

If you need to apply this to multiple peers, repeat the `neighbor` block for each peer IP address within the same group or create separate groups as needed.

For more control over route advertisement, you can optionally combine this with a route policy:

```cli
configure router policy-options
    policy-statement <policy-name>
        entry 10
            from protocol static
            from prefix 0.0.0.0/0 exact
