To prevent BGP peers from using 4-byte autonomous system numbers on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration command:

```
configure router bgp 
    disable-capability-negotiation
```

This command disables BGP capability negotiation, which includes the negotiation of 4-byte ASN support. After applying this configuration and resetting the BGP session, the peer will only support basic IPv4 routing exchanges without 4-byte ASN capabilities.
