To prevent BGP peers from using 4-byte autonomous system numbers on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

1. To disable 4-byte ASN globally for all BGP peers:
```
configure router bgp
    disable-4byte-asn
exit
```

2. To disable 4-byte ASN for a specific BGP group:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    disable-4byte-asn
exit
```

3. To disable 4-byte ASN for a specific neighbor:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    disable-4byte-asn
exit
```

Choose the appropriate level (global, group, or neighbor) based on where you want to apply the restriction.
