Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure a Nokia router to strictly support only IPv4 routing exchanges with a BGP peer by preventing new capability negotiations, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <peer-ip-address>
            disable-capability-negotiation
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<peer-ip-address>` with the IP address of your BGP peer. This configuration will ensure that only IPv4 routing exchanges are supported and new capability negotiations are prevented with the specified peer.
