Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure a Nokia router to strictly support IPv4 routing exchanges with BGP peer 192.0.2.1 without negotiating any new capabilities, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor 192.0.2.1
            disable-capability-negotiation
            no extended-nh-encoding
            no outbound-route-filtering
            no vpn-ipv4
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name. This configuration:
1. Disables capability negotiation entirely with the specific peer
2. Explicitly turns off extended next-hop encoding
3. Disables outbound route filtering
4. Ensures VPN-IPv4 is not enabled

The peer will now only support basic IPv4 routing exchanges without any additional capabilities.
