To configure a Nokia router to remove both standard and large BGP communities when advertising routes to a peer, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            disable-communities standard large
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the specific peer's IP address. This configuration will prevent the router from sending both standard and large BGP communities to the specified peer.
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router to remove both standard and large BGP communities when advertising routes to a peer?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to remove both standard and large BGP communities when advertising routes to a peer, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            disable-communities standard large
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the specific peer's IP address. This configuration will prevent the router from sending both standard and large BGP communities to the specified peer.
