## Proposed answer:
To configure BGP on a Nokia router to prevent immediate session teardown upon link failure detection, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        restart-time 300
        stale-routes-time 600
        enable-notification
    exit
    group <group-name>
        graceful-restart
            restart-time 300
            stale-routes-time 600
            enable-notification
        exit
        neighbor <neighbor-ip>
            graceful-restart
                restart-time 300
                stale-routes-time 600
                enable-notification
            exit
            hold-time 180
            keepalive 60
            no enable-peer-tracking
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Key configurations:
- `graceful-restart` is enabled globally and per peer to allow session recovery without tearing down
- Extended `restart-time` and `stale-routes-time` values provide sufficient recovery windows
- `enable-notification` allows graceful handling of error notifications
- Increased `hold-time` and `keepalive` intervals reduce false-positive failure detection
- `no enable-peer-tracking` prevents immediate session drops when routes flap

These settings ensure BGP sessions remain stable during transient link failures while still detecting actual outages.
