To prevent Nokia routers from installing both labeled and unlabeled BGP routes into RTM and FIB in the base router instance, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    no family label-ipv4
    no family label-ipv6
exit
```

This configuration removes support for the labeled IPv4 and IPv6 address families in the base BGP instance, preventing the installation of labeled routes while still allowing unlabeled routes (IPv4/IPv6) to be processed normally. 

If you need to selectively filter specific labeled routes while keeping others, you would need to create and apply appropriate route policies using the `import` or `export` commands with prefix lists or community filters.
