Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To prevent all BGP routes from being installed into RTM and FIB on a Nokia router's base router instance, you need to disable all BGP address families. Here's the CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    no family
exit
```

This command removes all BGP address family configurations, effectively preventing any BGP routes from being installed in the routing table (RTM) and forwarding information base (FIB).
