---
## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router to accept a maximum of 500 dynamic BGP sessions from remote peers within a BGP instance?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to accept a maximum of 500 dynamic BGP sessions within a BGP instance, use the following command:

```
configure router bgp dynamic-neighbor-limit 500
``` 

This command sets the maximum number of dynamic BGP sessions to 500 for the entire BGP instance.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
dynamic-neighbor-limit <peers>
no dynamic-neighbor-limit
FuncDef:
This command configures the maximum number of dynamic BGP sessions that will be accepted from remote peers associated with the entire BGP instance or a specific peer group. If accepting a new dynamic session would cause either the group limit or the instance limit to be exceeded, then the new session attempt is rejected and a Notification message is sent back to the remote peer.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'peers', 'Info': 'The maximum number of dynamic BGP sessions. Values-1 to 8192.'}
