Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To enable dynamic BGP session configuration for a peer group on Nokia routers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <peer-group-name>
        type peer
        dynamic-neighbor <subnet/mask> [local-address <ip-address>]
        family <address-family>
        no shutdown
```

Replace `<peer-group-name>` with your peer group name, `<subnet/mask>` with the subnet range where dynamic neighbors may establish sessions, and `<ip-address>` with the local interface IP if needed. Specify the appropriate `<address-family>` (e.g., ipv4, ipv6, vpn-ipv4, etc.).

For example:
```
configure router bgp
    group DYNAMIC_PEERS
        type peer
        dynamic-neighbor 192.0.2.0/24 local-address 203.0.113.1
        family ipv4
        no shutdown
```
