Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To enable dynamic BGP session configuration for a peer group on Nokia routers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <peer-group-name>
        type peer
        peer-as <as-number>
        dynamic-neighbors <interface-name> [max-peers <max-value>]
        family <address-family>
        no shutdown
```

Replace:
- `<peer-group-name>` with your peer group name
- `<as-number>` with the AS number of your peers
- `<interface-name>` with the interface where dynamic neighbors will be discovered
- `<max-value>` with the maximum number of peers allowed (optional)
- `<address-family>` with the appropriate address family (e.g., ipv4, ipv6, vpn-ipv4)

Example:
```
configure router bgp
    group DYNAMIC_PEERS
        type peer
        peer-as 65001
        dynamic-neighbors "lag-1" max-peers 50
        family ipv4
        no shutdown
```
