    "CLIs": [
        "graceful-restart",
        "undo graceful-restart"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "BGP view"
    ],
    "ParaDef": null,
    "Examples": [
        [
            "<HUAWEI> system-view",
            "[~HUAWEI] bgp 100",
            "[*HUAWEI-bgp] graceful-restart"
        ]
    ],
    "ExtraInfo": "Usage Scenario\nA BGP restart causes traffic interruption. To prevent traffic interruption, run the graceful-restart command on a BGP speaker to enable GR globally. This enables all the peers specified on the BGP speaker to perform GR during a BGP restart.\nConfiguration Impact\nEnabling or disabling GR may delete and reestablish all BGP sessions and instances.\nFollow-up Procedure\nRun the graceful-restart timer wait-for-rib command to set the time for waiting for the End-Of-RIB flag."
}
