## User question:
How to configure Nokia routers to import all received VPN-IP routes into the dummy VRF for BGP next-hop resolution?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to import all received VPN-IP routes into the dummy VRF for BGP next-hop resolution, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        vpn-apply-import
        next-hop-resolution
            labeled-routes
                transport-tunnel
                    family vpn
                        resolution-filter bgp
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enables the application of base BGP import policies to VPN routes (`vpn-apply-import`)
2. Configures next-hop resolution for VPN routes that aren't imported into any VPRN service
3. Uses BGP tunnels for next-hop resolution of these routes

The VPN routes will now be available in the base routing instance for next-hop resolution purposes while still being properly handled as VPN routes.
