Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To verify that the last ASN in the AS_PATH of all routes received from an EBGP peer matches the configured peer-as value, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    enforce-first-as
exit
```

This command ensures that all routes received from EBGP peers will be checked to confirm that the most recent ASN in their AS_PATH matches the configured `peer-as` value. If there's a mismatch, the session will be reset (or the route treated as withdrawn if update fault tolerance is enabled). 

The command can also be applied at the group or neighbor level if you need more granular control:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    enforce-first-as
exit
```

Or:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    enforce-first-as
exit
```
------------
