Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure a Nokia router to only accept labeled routes for BGP next-hop resolution when the transport tunnels are explicitly tagged with an admin-tag, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel family label-ipv4
                admin-tag 100
            exit
            transport-tunnel family label-ipv6
                admin-tag 100
            exit
            no allow-static
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `admin-tag 100` with your desired tag value. This configuration ensures:
1. Only labeled routes (both IPv4 and IPv6) are accepted for next-hop resolution
2. Transport tunnels must have the specified admin-tag (100 in this example)
3. Static routes are excluded from next-hop resolution
------------
