To enable the updated BGP error handling procedures on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    error-handling
exit
```

This command enables the updated BGP error handling procedures at the global BGP level. You can also apply it at the group or neighbor level if needed by navigating to those contexts (`config>router>bgp>group` or `config>router>bgp>group>neighbor`) before entering the `error-handling` command.
