            "[*HUAWEI-bgp] peer 10.1.1.1 as-number 100",
            "[*HUAWEI-bgp] ipv4-family vpnv4",
            "[*HUAWEI-bgp-af-vpnv4] peer 10.1.1.1 enable",
            "[*HUAWEI-bgp-af-vpnv4] peer 10.1.1.1 route-policy test-policy export"
        ]
    ],
    "ExtraInfo": "Usage Scenario\nAfter a route-policy is created, the peer route-policy export command is used to apply a Route-Policy to a peer so that the routes advertised to the peer can be controlled. To be specific, only the necessary routes are advertised to the peer. In this manner, route management is implemented, the scale of the routing table is reduced, and fewer network resources are consumed.\nIn a bit-error-triggered protection switching scenario, if you want to use the local preference or MED attribute specified in the export routing policy no matter whether bit errors occur, run the peer route-policy export ignore-bit-error command.\nPrerequisites\nIf the command specifies a route-policy that does not exist, use the route-policy command to create the route-policy.\nConfiguration Impact\nIf the peer route-policy command is run for a peer group, all the members of the peer group inherit the configuration.\nThe peer route-policy command is mutually exclusive with the peer route-filter commands.\nBinding a route-policy after a BGP peer relationship is established may cause peer flapping."
}
