## User question:
How to configure Nokia routers to enable extended community-based BGP filtering in outbound route filtering?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure extended community-based BGP filtering for outbound route filtering on Nokia routers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            family vpn-ipv4
            export "extended-community-policy"
exit
```

Where:
- `<group-name>` is your BGP group name
- `<ip-address>` is the neighbor IP address
- `"extended-community-policy"` is your predefined route policy that includes extended community matching criteria

Make sure you've first created the appropriate policy in the policy-options context that matches against extended communities. For example:

```
configure router policy-options
    begin
    policy-statement "extended-community-policy"
        entry 10
            from community "target:12345:100"
            action reject
        exit
    commit
exit
```

This configuration applies extended community-based filtering to outbound VPN-IPv4 routes. Adjust the family type (vpn-ipv4/vpn-ipv6) and policy details as needed for your specific requirements.
