To configure next-hop resolution for unlabeled IPv6 BGP routes using shortcut tunnels on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        next-hop-resolution
            shortcut-tunnel
                family ipv6
                    resolution-filter bgp ldp rsvp sr-isis sr-ospf sr-policy sr-te
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enters the BGP context under router configuration
2. Configures next-hop resolution with shortcut tunnels
3. Specifies IPv6 as the address family
4. Defines the allowed tunnel types for resolution (BGP, LDP, RSVP, and various Segment Routing tunnel types)

Adjust the `resolution-filter` parameters based on which specific tunnel types you want to allow for next-hop resolution.
