Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
Here are the CLI configuration commands to configure a Nokia router to report both IPv6 unicast (labeled) and IPv4 VPN (SAFI 128) address families to a BMP monitoring station:

```cli
# Configure BMP station
configure
    bmp
        station "BMP_STATION_NAME"
            connection
                # Specify BMP station IP/port here
                no shutdown
            exit
            report-local-routes
            route-monitoring pre-policy post-policy
            family label-ipv6
            family vpn-ipv4
            no shutdown
        exit
    exit

# Enable required BGP address families and features
configure router bgp
    rapid-update label-ipv6 vpn-ipv4
    advertise-ipv6-next-hops label-ipv6 vpn-ipv4
    no shutdown
exit
```

Replace `"BMP_STATION_NAME"` with your actual BMP monitoring station name and configure the connection parameters under the `connection` context with the appropriate IP address and port number for your monitoring station.
