To create a BGP peer group named "EU-West-1" on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group "EU-West-1"
    exit
exit
```

This creates a basic BGP peer group. You can further customize the group by adding parameters like `type`, `connect-retry`, `hold-time`, etc., under the group context if needed. For example:

```
configure router bgp
    group "EU-West-1"
        type external
        connect-retry 30
        hold-time 180
    exit
exit
```
