Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure a Nokia router to enforce a locally-defined restart time of 300 seconds for all AFI/SAFI included in the peer's GR capability during long-lived graceful restart, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        restart-time 300
        long-lived
    exit
exit
```

This configuration sets the BGP graceful restart restart-time to 300 seconds and enables long-lived graceful restart for all address families supported by the peer's GR capability. The changes apply globally under the BGP context.
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
"How to configure a Nokia router to enforce a locally-defined restart time of 300 seconds for all AFI/SAFI included in the peer's GR capability during long-lived graceful restart?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to enforce a locally-defined restart time of 300 seconds for all AFI/SAFI included in the peer's GR capability during long-lived graceful restart, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        restart-time 300
        long-lived
    exit
exit
```

This configuration sets the BGP graceful restart restart-time to 300 seconds and enables long-lived graceful restart for all address families supported by the peer's GR capability. The changes apply globally under the BGP context.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
helper-override-restart-time <seconds>
no helper-override-restart-time
FuncDef:
This command overrides the restart-time advertised by a peer (in its GR capability) with a locally-configured value. This override applies only to AFI/SAFI that were included in the GR capability of the peer. The restart-time is always zero for AFI/SAFI not included in the GR capability. This command is useful if the local router wants to force LLGR phase to begin after a set time for all protected AFI/SAFI.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'seconds', 'Info': 'The locally-imposed restart time for all AFI/SAFI included in the peer s GR capability. Values-0 to 4095.'}
