Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure a Nokia router to locally impose an LLGR stale time of 3600 seconds, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        long-lived
            stale-routes-time 3600
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration sets the local LLGR stale routes time to 3600 seconds, which will override any peer-advertised values. The setting applies globally to all BGP peers under the router BGP instance.
