---
## User question:
"How to configure Nokia routers to locally impose an LLGR stale time of 3600 seconds when overriding a peer's advertised value?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to locally impose an LLGR stale time of 3600 seconds, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        long-lived
            stale-routes-time 3600
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration sets the local LLGR stale routes time to 3600 seconds, which will override any peer-advertised values. The setting applies globally to all BGP peers under the router BGP instance.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
helper-override-stale-time <seconds>
no helper-override-stale-time
FuncDef:
This command overrides the LLGR stale-time advertised by a peer (in its LLGR capability) with a locally-configured value. When configured in thelong-livedconfiguration context,helper-override-stale-timeapplies to all AFI/SAFI in the advertised LLGR capability except for any AFI/SAFI with a family-specific override. A family-specific override is configured with thehelper-override-stale-timecommand in a family context.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'seconds', 'Info': 'Specifies the locally imposed LLGR stale time in seconds. Values-0 to 16777215.'}
