To configure a Nokia router to impose a local LLGR stale time of 3600 seconds while overriding the peer-advertised value, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        long-lived
            stale-routes-time 3600
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration enables long-lived graceful restart (LLGR) and sets the stale routes time to 3600 seconds at the global BGP level. The setting will override any peer-advertised values.
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
"How to configure Nokia routers to impose a local LLGR stale time of 3600 seconds when overriding the peer-advertised value?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to impose a local LLGR stale time of 3600 seconds while overriding the peer-advertised value, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        long-lived
            stale-routes-time 3600
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration enables long-lived graceful restart (LLGR) and sets the stale routes time to 3600 seconds at the global BGP level. The setting will override any peer-advertised values.
