Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To prevent BGP from considering the resolved distance to the next-hop when comparing routes with the same NLRI from base router BGP peers, configure the following:

```
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        as-path-ignore ipv4 ipv6
exit
```

This command disables the AS path length comparison in the BGP best path selection process for both IPv4 and IPv6 routes. This ensures that the resolved distance to the next-hop is not considered when evaluating routes with the same NLRI.
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
How to configure Nokia routers to prevent BGP from considering the resolved distance to the next-hop when comparing routes with the same NLRI from base router BGP peers?
---
## Proposed answer:
To prevent BGP from considering the resolved distance to the next-hop when comparing routes with the same NLRI from base router BGP peers, configure the following:

```
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        as-path-ignore ipv4 ipv6
exit
```

This command disables the AS path length comparison in the BGP best path selection process for both IPv4 and IPv6 routes. This ensures that the resolved distance to the next-hop is not considered when evaluating routes with the same NLRI.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
ignore-nh-metric
no ignore-nh-metric
FuncDef:
This command instructs BGP to disregard the resolved distance to the BGP next-hop in its decision process for selecting the best route to a destination. When configured in theconfig>router>bgp>best-path-selectioncontext, this command applies to the comparison of two BGP routes with the same NLRI learned from base router BGP peers. When configured in theconfig>service>vprncontext, this command applies to the comparison of two BGP-VPN routes for the same IP prefix imported into the VPRN from the base router BGP instance. When configured in theconfig>service>vprn>bgp>best-path-selectioncontext, this command applies to the comparison of two BGP routes for the same IP prefix learned from VPRN BGP peers.
ParaDef:
No ParaDef found
