To configure the Nokia router BGP to apply the route policy "cust123-inbound-filter" for processing incoming routes from a specific peer, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <peer-ip-address> import "cust123-inbound-filter"
```

or if applying at the group level:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> import "cust123-inbound-filter"
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<peer-ip-address>` with the specific peer's IP address. The policy name should be enclosed in quotes as shown.
