## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia routers to immediately send BGP UPDATE messages when sessions are established with peers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    no disable-capability-negotiation
exit
```

This ensures BGP capability negotiation remains enabled (default behavior), allowing the router to immediately exchange BGP UPDATE messages upon session establishment. 

For more granular control at the group or neighbor level:
```
configure router bgp group "GROUP_NAME"
    no disable-capability-negotiation
exit
```

Or:
```
configure router bgp group "GROUP_NAME" neighbor "IP_ADDRESS"
    no disable-capability-negotiation
exit
