To configure the Nokia router to declare a TCP connection down after missing 15 consecutive keepalives, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    hold-time 225
    keepalive 15
exit
```

These settings ensure:
- Keepalives are sent every 15 seconds (default interval)
- The connection will be declared down if no keepalive response is received within 225 seconds (15 keepalive intervals × 15 seconds each)

The hold-time must be set to 3 times the keepalive interval according to BGP specifications, hence 15 × 3 = 45 would be the minimum, but setting it to 15 × 15 = 225 ensures exactly 15 missed keepalives will trigger the connection drop.
