Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure the Nokia router to declare a TCP connection down after missing 5 consecutive keepalives, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure
bmp
station
connection
tcp-keepalive
keep-interval 75
exit all
```

This configuration sets the keepalive interval to 75 seconds (5 missed keepalives × default 15-second interval = 75 seconds). When 5 consecutive keepalives are missed (after 75 seconds), the TCP connection will be declared down.
------------
