To configure the BGP keepalive timer to 60 seconds on a Nokia router, use the following CLI command:

```
configure router bgp keepalive 60
```

If you need to apply this setting at the group or neighbor level instead of globally, navigate to the respective context and execute the same command there. For example:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> keepalive 60
```

or

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <neighbor-ip> keepalive 60
```
