## User question:
Configure Nokia routers to advertise a maximum of 8 labeled-unicast IPv6 paths per prefix and disable receiving multiple paths capability.
---
## Proposed answer:
Here are the CLI configuration commands to limit labeled-unicast IPv6 paths to 8 per prefix and disable receiving multiple paths:

```
configure router bgp
    no multipath
    exit
```

Or alternatively, to explicitly set the limit to 8 while effectively disabling multipath reception:

```
configure router bgp
    multipath 1
    exit
```

Note: The first option (`no multipath`) completely disables multipath functionality, while the second option sets the maximum paths to 1 (effectively single-path). Both approaches achieve the goal of preventing multiple path reception. There isn't a specific command to limit just the receive capability while keeping transmit capability, so these are the closest available configurations.
