To configure a Nokia router to advertise up to 8 labeled-unicast IPv6 paths per prefix and negotiate to receive multiple paths, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    family label-ipv6
    add-paths
        label-ipv6 send 8 receive
    exit
exit
```

If you need to apply this configuration at the group or neighbor level instead of globally, use these variations:

For a BGP group:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    family label-ipv6
    add-paths
        label-ipv6 send 8 receive
    exit
exit
```

For a specific BGP neighbor:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    family label-ipv6
    add-paths
        label-ipv6 send 8 receive
    exit
exit
```
