## Proposed answer:
To enable LDP tunneling for next-hop resolution of /32 IPv4 FECs in BGP labeled routes on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        next-hop-resolution
            labeled-routes
                transport-tunnel
                    family label-ipv4
                        resolution-filter ldp
                        resolution filter
```

This configuration:
1. Enters the BGP labeled-IPv4 routes context
2. Enables LDP as the tunnel type for next-hop resolution
3. Sets the resolution mode to use only the filtered tunnel types (LDP in this case)

The router will now use LDP tunnels for resolving next-hops of /32 IPv4 FECs in BGP labeled routes.
