## Proposed answer:
To enable the configuration context for handling the link-bandwidth extended community attached to specific BGP routes on a Nokia router, you need to configure BGP import policies that process these communities. Here are the relevant CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    import "link-bw-policy"
exit
```

Where "link-bw-policy" is a predefined policy that includes actions to handle the link-bandwidth extended community. You would create this policy in the `config>router>policy-options` context first. 

For example:
```
configure router policy-options
    begin
    policy-statement "link-bw-policy"
        entry 10
            from community "link-bw-community"
            action accept
            exit
        exit
    commit
exit
```

Note that the actual policy configuration would depend on your specific requirements for processing the link-bandwidth extended community.
