How to configure Nokia routers to use the IP address 192.0.2.1 as the source for BGP communication within a group?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to use the IP address 192.0.2.1 as the source for BGP communication within a group, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        local-address 192.0.2.1
```

Replace `<group-name>` with the actual name of your BGP group. This sets the local address for all BGP communications within that group to 192.0.2.1.
