To configure the Nokia router to use the interface named "core-link-1" as the source address for BGP communication within a group, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        local-address core-link-1
```

Replace `<group-name>` with the actual name of your BGP group. This command sets the source address for all BGP communications within the specified group to the IP address assigned to the "core-link-1" interface.
