Here are the CLI configuration commands to configure a Nokia router with local AS number 65535 and both private and no-prepend-global-as options enabled for BGP:

```
configure router bgp
    local-as 65535 private no-prepend-global-as
exit
```

This configuration:
- Sets the local AS number to 65535
- Enables the `private` option to hide the local AS in paths learned from the peering
- Enables the `no-prepend-global-as` option to hide the global AS in paths announced to BGP peers

The configuration is applied at the global BGP level, affecting all BGP groups and neighbors unless overridden at those levels.
