## User question:
"How to set the BGP local-preference attribute to 200 on a Nokia router when it is not specified in incoming routes?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To set the BGP local-preference attribute to 200 when it is not specified in incoming routes, use the following CLI command:

```
configure router bgp local-preference 200
```

This command will apply the local-preference value of 200 to all incoming BGP routes that do not already have this attribute specified.
