To configure the BGP local preference value to 200 on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    local-preference 200
exit
```

This sets the BGP local preference attribute to 200 globally for all routes. You can also apply this at the group or neighbor level if needed:

For a specific BGP group:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    local-preference 200
exit
```

For a specific BGP neighbor:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    local-preference 200
exit
```
