## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router to advertise the MED path attribute with a value of 15000 when it's not already set in BGP?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to advertise the MED path attribute with a value of 15000 when it's not already set in BGP, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    default-med 15000
exit
```

This command sets the default MED value to 15000 for all BGP routes that don't already have a MED attribute. The router will apply this value when advertising routes to its BGP peers.
