To configure the TTL value to 128 for EBGP packets when the peer is multiple hops away on a Nokia router, use the following CLI command:

```
configure router bgp multihop 128
```

If you need to configure this at the group or neighbor level instead of globally, the commands would be:

For a BGP group:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> multihop 128
```

For a specific neighbor:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> multihop 128
```
