To configure a Nokia router to encode type/subtype in advertised MVPN routes as 0x010b, you need to enable the MVPN address family in BGP. Here are the CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    family mvpn-ipv4
exit
```

This configuration enables the MVPN-IPv4 address family, which will advertise MVPN routes with the standard type/subtype encoding (0x010b for PIM-SSM join synch routes). No additional explicit configuration is needed for the 0x010b encoding as this is the default behavior when MVPN-IPv4 family is enabled.
