## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router to preserve the original BGP next-hop for both IPv4 and IPv6 labeled routes when advertising to peers in a specific BGP group?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to preserve the original BGP next-hop for both IPv4 and IPv6 labeled routes when advertising to peers in a specific BGP group, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    next-hop-unchanged label-ipv4 label-ipv6
```

Replace `<group-name>` with the name of your BGP group. This command ensures the original next-hop is preserved for both IPv4 and IPv6 labeled routes when advertising to peers in the specified group.
---
