To enable optimal route reflection (ORR) in BGP on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    cluster <cluster-id> orr-location <location-id> [allow-local-fallback]
```

Replace `<cluster-id>` with your route reflector cluster ID (e.g., `1.1.1.1`) and `<location-id>` with the optimal route reflection location index (a value between 1-16). The optional `allow-local-fallback` parameter allows advertising the best reachable BGP path from the RR's own topology if no routes are available from the client's ORR location perspective.

Example:
