To configure a Nokia router to enable BGP peer acceptance of filter lists for outbound routes, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            outbound-route-filtering
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the peer's IP address. This enables outbound route filtering for the specified BGP neighbor, allowing the peer to accept filter lists for outbound routes.
