To enable entropy label capability for BGP tunnels on a Nokia router, you need to configure labeled-unicast address family settings. Here are the relevant CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    family label-ipv4
exit
```

This command enters the context for configuring next-hop-resolution options for labeled-unicast IPv4 routes, which includes enabling entropy label capability for BGP tunnels. The exact implementation of entropy labels may depend on additional platform-specific capabilities that aren't detailed in the provided reference content.
