To enable automatic adjustment of TCP session MTU based on ICMP feedback in Nokia routers, you need to configure Path MTU Discovery (PMTUD) at the BGP level. While the specific PMTUD configuration isn't shown in your provided content, the typical Nokia SR OS command would be:

```
configure router bgp path-mtu-discovery
```

This enables BGP to automatically adjust TCP session MTU sizes based on ICMP "Fragmentation Needed" messages received from the network path.

Note: If you need to apply this to specific BGP groups or neighbors, you would navigate to those contexts first before applying the command. For example:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> path-mtu-discovery
```
