To configure the Nokia router to send a warning message when receiving 5000 IPv6 routes from a peer at 80% threshold without terminating the BGP session, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <peer-ip>
            family ipv6
                prefix-limit ipv6 5000 threshold 80 log-only
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<peer-ip>` with the IP address of the BGP peer. This configuration will trigger a warning when the received IPv6 routes reach 4000 (80% of 5000) and again when reaching 5000, while keeping the BGP session active.
