## User question:
How to configure Nokia router to accept dynamic BGP sessions from peers within the 192.168.10.0/24 subnet?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to accept dynamic BGP sessions from peers within the 192.168.10.0/24 subnet, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group DYNAMIC_PEERS
        type external
        peer-as <remote-peer-as-number>
        neighbor 192.168.10.0/24
            no shutdown
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<remote-peer-as-number>` with the actual autonomous system number of your BGP peers. This configuration creates a BGP group named `DYNAMIC_PEERS` for external peers and allows dynamic sessions from any peer in the 192.168.10.0/24 subnet. The `no shutdown` command ensures the neighbor configuration is active.
