To configure the primary IPv6 address as 2001:db8::1 for BGP optimal route reflection on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        cluster 2001:db8::1 orr-location 1
        family ipv6
        no shutdown
    exit
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Sets the BGP cluster ID to the IPv6 address 2001:db8::1
2. Enables optimal route reflection with location ID 1
3. Enables IPv6 address family support
4. Ensures BGP is not administratively shut down
