## User question:
How long will Nokia router wait before removing stale VPN-IP routes from RIB-IN after sending a Route-Refresh, when configured with a value of 15 minutes?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure the Nokia router to wait 15 minutes before removing stale VPN-IP routes from RIB-IN after sending a Route-Refresh, use the following command:

```
configure router bgp purge-timer 15
``` 

This sets the purge timer to 15 minutes (900 seconds). The router will maintain stale VPN-IP routes for this duration before purging them if they aren't refreshed.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
purge-timer <minutes>
no purge-timer
FuncDef:
When the system sends a VPN-IP Route-Refresh to a peer it sets all the VPN-IP routes received from that peer (in the RIB-IN) to stale and starts the purge-timer. If the routes are not updated (refreshed) before the purge-timer has expired then the routes are removed.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'minutes', 'Info': 'Specifies the maximum time before stale routes are purged. Values-1 to 60.'}
---
