Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure a Nokia router to remove private ASNs in BGP updates while preserving private ASN 64512 when it matches the peer's AS number, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            peer-as 64512
            remove-private skip-peer-as
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the neighbor's IP address. This configuration will:
1. Set the peer AS to 64512
2. Remove private ASNs from AS paths in outgoing updates
3. Preserve ASN 64512 in the AS path when it matches the peer's AS number
------------
