To configure your Nokia router to strip private AS numbers from BGP updates while preserving private AS 64512 when it matches the peer's AS number, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            peer-as 64512
            remove-private skip-peer-as
exit all
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the neighbor's IP address. The `skip-peer-as` parameter ensures that AS 64512 is preserved when it matches the peer's AS number, while other private AS numbers in the path will be stripped.
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router to strip private AS numbers from BGP updates while preserving private AS64512 when it matches the peer's AS number?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure your Nokia router to strip private AS numbers from BGP updates while preserving private AS 64512 when it matches the peer's AS number, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            peer-as 64512
            remove-private skip-peer-as
exit all
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the neighbor's IP address. The `skip-peer-as` parameter ensures that AS 64512 is preserved when it matches the peer's AS number, while other private AS numbers in the path will be stripped.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
remove-private [ limited ] [ skip-peer-as ]
no remove-private
FuncDef:
This command allows private AS numbers to be removed from the AS path before advertising them to BGP peers.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'limited', 'Info': 'This optional keyword removes private ASNs up to the first public ASN encountered. It then stops removing private ASNs.'}
{'Parameters': 'skip-peer-as', 'Info': 'This optional keyword causes this command to not remove a private ASN from the AS-Path if that ASN is the same as the BGP peer AS number.'}
