Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure a Nokia router to allow only RSVP and SR-ISIS tunnel types for resolving BGP unlabeled routes, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        next-hop-resolution
            shortcut-tunnels
                family ipv4
                    resolution-filter
                        rsvp
                        sr-isis
                        no bgp
                        no ldp
                        no sr-ospf
                    exit
                exit
            exit
            labeled-routes
                transport-tunnel
                    family ipv4
                        resolution-filter
                            rsvp
                            sr-isis
                            no bgp
                            no ldp
                            no sr-ospf
                        exit
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration ensures that only RSVP and Segment Routing IS-IS tunnels are used for resolving BGP unlabeled routes, while explicitly disabling other tunnel types (BGP, LDP, and OSPF Segment Routing).
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
"How to configure a Nokia router to allow only RSVP and SR-ISIS tunnel types for resolving BGP unlabeled routes?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to allow only RSVP and SR-ISIS tunnel types for resolving BGP unlabeled routes, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        next-hop-resolution
            shortcut-tunnels
                family ipv4
                    resolution-filter
                        rsvp
                        sr-isis
                        no bgp
                        no ldp
                        no sr-ospf
                    exit
                exit
            exit
            labeled-routes
                transport-tunnel
                    family ipv4
                        resolution-filter
                            rsvp
                            sr-isis
                            no bgp
                            no ldp
                            no sr-ospf
                        exit
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration ensures that only RSVP and Segment Routing IS-IS tunnels are used for resolving BGP unlabeled routes, while explicitly disabling other tunnel types (BGP, LDP, and OSPF Segment Routing).
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
resolution-filter [ bgp ] [ ldp ] [ rsvp ] [ sr-isis ] [ sr-ospf ] [ sr-policy ] [ sr-te ]
FuncDef:
This command configures the subset of tunnel types that can be used in the resolution of BGP unlabeled routes.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'bgp', 'Info': 'Selects the BGP label route tunnel type.'}
{'Parameters': 'ldp', 'Info': 'Selects the LDP tunnel type.'}
{'Parameters': 'rsvp', 'Info': 'Selects the RSVP-TE tunnel type.'}
{'Parameters': 'sr-isis', 'Info': 'Selects the SR tunnel type programmed by an IS-IS instance in TTM.'}
{'Parameters': 'sr-ospf', 'Info': 'Selects the SR tunnel type programmed by an OSPF instance in TTM.'}
{'Parameters': 'sr-policy', 'Info': 'Selects the SR tunnel type programmed by an SR policy instance in TTM.'}
{'Parameters': 'sr-te', 'Info': 'Selects the SR tunnel type programmed by a TE instance in TTM.'}
