## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia routers to allow only RSVP-TE and Segment Routing tunnels programmed by IS-IS for resolving BGP unlabeled routes, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    no family label-ipv4
    no family label-ipv6
    export "RSVP_SR_POLICY"
exit

configure router policy-options
    begin
    policy-statement "RSVP_SR_POLICY"
        entry 10
            from protocol isis
            from tunnel-type rsvp-te segment-routing
            accept
        exit
        default-action reject
    commit
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Disables BGP labeled address families to ensure only unlabeled routes are processed
2. Creates an export policy that:
   - Accepts routes only from IS-IS protocol
   - Restricts resolution to RSVP-TE and Segment Routing tunnels
   - Rejects all other routes by default

The policy ensures BGP unlabeled routes can only be resolved via ISIS-programmed RSVP-TE or Segment Routing tunnels.
