Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure a Nokia router to bind BGP label routes only to specific tunnel types under the resolution-filter, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family label-ipv4
                    resolution-filter bgp ldp rsvp
                exit
                family label-ipv6
                    resolution-filter bgp ldp rsvp
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `bgp ldp rsvp` with your desired subset of tunnel types (e.g., `sr-isis`, `sr-ospf`, `sr-policy`, or `sr-te`) based on which tunnel types you want to allow for BGP label route resolution.
