## User question:
How to configure Nokia router to bind BGP label routes only to the subset of tunnel types specified under resolution-filter?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to bind BGP label routes only to specific tunnel types under the resolution-filter, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family label-ipv4
                    resolution-filter bgp ldp rsvp
                exit
                family label-ipv6
                    resolution-filter bgp ldp rsvp
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `bgp ldp rsvp` with your desired subset of tunnel types (e.g., `sr-isis`, `sr-ospf`, `sr-policy`, or `sr-te`) based on which tunnel types you want to allow for BGP label route resolution.
