To configure BGP label route resolution binding to only a subset of tunnel types specified under resolution-filter, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family label-ipv4
                    resolution-filter bgp
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enters the BGP labeled-routes transport-tunnel context
2. Selects the label-ipv4 address family
3. Configures the resolution-filter to bind only to BGP tunnels

Replace `label-ipv4` with `label-ipv6` if you need to configure this for IPv6 labeled routes. You can also add other tunnel types to the resolution-filter as needed.
