Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure BGP next-hop resolution to only bind to tunnel types specified in the resolution-filter on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family label-ipv4
                    resolution-filter
                        type [tunnel-type]
                exit
                family label-ipv6
                    resolution-filter
                        type [tunnel-type]
                exit
                family vpn
                    resolution-filter
                        type [tunnel-type]
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `[tunnel-type]` with the specific tunnel types you want to allow (e.g., "ldp", "rsvp", "sr-te"). This configuration restricts BGP next-hop resolution to only use the specified tunnel types for each address family.
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
How to configure Nokia router's BGP next-hop resolution to only bind to tunnel types specified in the resolution-filter?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure BGP next-hop resolution to only bind to tunnel types specified in the resolution-filter on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family label-ipv4
                    resolution-filter
                        type [tunnel-type]
                exit
                family label-ipv6
                    resolution-filter
                        type [tunnel-type]
                exit
                family vpn
                    resolution-filter
                        type [tunnel-type]
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `[tunnel-type]` with the specific tunnel types you want to allow (e.g., "ldp", "rsvp", "sr-te"). This configuration restricts BGP next-hop resolution to only use the specified tunnel types for each address family.
