Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure BGP next-hop resolution to only bind to specific tunnel types in the resolution-filter, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family [label-ipv4|label-ipv6|vpn]
                    resolution-filter
                        [bgp|ldp|rsvp|sr-te|none]
```

For example, to allow only BGP tunnels for labeled IPv4 routes:
```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family label-ipv4
                    resolution-filter
                        bgp
```

Or for multiple tunnel types (e.g., RSVP and SR-TE):
```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family label-ipv4
                    resolution-filter
                        rsvp
                        sr-te
```
------------
