To configure a Nokia router to use the VPRN service named 'customer-backbone' for connecting to a BMP monitoring station, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure
    bmp
        station "monitoring-station"
            connection
                router service-name "customer-backbone"
                station-address <ip-address> port <port>
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `<ip-address>` with the IP address of your BMP monitoring station and `<port>` with the appropriate TCP port number. This configuration ensures the BMP station connection traverses through the specified VPRN service.
