Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure a Nokia router's BGP next-hop resolution for labeled routes to use IGP route table lookup instead of tunnel signaling protocols, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family label-ipv4
                    resolution-filter
                        no bgp
                    exit
                exit
                family label-ipv6
                    resolution-filter
                        no bgp
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration disables BGP tunneling (`no bgp`) for both IPv4 and IPv6 labeled routes under the resolution filter, forcing the router to use IGP route table lookups for next-hop resolution.
