## User question:
How to configure a secondary IPv4 address 192.168.10.20 for BGP optimal route reflection on a Nokia router?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a secondary IPv4 address 192.168.10.20 for BGP optimal route reflection on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        local-address 192.168.10.20
        family ipv4
        no shutdown
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name. This configuration sets the local BGP session address to 192.168.10.20 and enables IPv4 address family support for the group.
