To add a secondary IPv4 address 192.168.10.20 for BGP optimal route reflection on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        local-address 192.168.10.20
        no shutdown
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your specific BGP group name where the route reflector is configured. This will configure the secondary IP address as the local address for BGP communications within that group.
