To configure the secondary IPv6 address 2001:db8::2 for BGP optimal route reflection on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    interface "interface-name" 
        address 2001:db8::2/64 secondary
    exit
    bgp
        group "group-name"
            family ipv6
            neighbor 2001:db8::2
                cluster 1.2.3.4
                route-reflector-client
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `interface-name` with your actual interface name and `group-name` with your BGP group name. Adjust the cluster ID (`1.2.3.4`) as needed for your route reflector configuration.
