Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure your Nokia router to include the link-bandwidth extended community in unlabeled unicast IPv6 routes advertised to EBGP peers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            send-to-ebgp ipv6
exit all
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your specific BGP group name. This configuration enables the advertisement of the link-bandwidth extended community for IPv6 routes to EBGP peers within the specified group.
