To administratively disable a BGP neighbor on a Nokia router without removing its configuration, use the `shutdown` command under the specific neighbor context:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            shutdown
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the neighbor's IP address. This will disable the BGP session while preserving all configuration parameters. To re-enable the neighbor later, use the `no shutdown` command in the same context.
