## Proposed answer:
To enable Segment Routing tunnels from IS-IS instances for BGP next-hop resolution on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family label-ipv4
                    resolution-filter
                        bgp
                    exit
                exit
                family label-ipv6
                    resolution-filter
                        bgp
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration enables BGP to use Segment Routing tunnels (via IS-IS) for resolving next-hops of labeled IPv4 and IPv6 routes. The `bgp` command under each family's `resolution-filter` context specifies that BGP-labeled routes should be used for next-hop resolution.
