## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to allow BGP to use Segment Routing tunnels from the lowest preference IS-IS instance for next-hop resolution, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel family label-ipv4
                isis-instance 1 preference 255
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enters the BGP next-hop resolution context
2. Configures labeled routes to use IS-IS instance 1 (the lowest preference instance)
3. Sets a high preference value (255) to ensure it's used as the last resort

The router will now prefer other tunnel types first but fall back to the specified IS-IS instance when needed.
