## User question:
How to configure Nokia routers to use Segment Routing tunnels from the lowest preference OSPF instance for BGP next-hop resolution?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia routers to use Segment Routing tunnels from the lowest preference OSPF instance for BGP next-hop resolution, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family label-ipv4
                    resolution-filter
                        sr-isis
                            preference 255
                        sr-ospf
                            preference 254
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration sets up BGP next-hop resolution for labeled IPv4 routes, giving SR-ISIS tunnels higher preference (lower numerical value) than SR-OSPF tunnels. The lower preference value (higher numerical value) for SR-OSPF ensures it will only be used when SR-ISIS tunnels are unavailable.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
sr-ospf
no sr-ospf
FuncDef:
This command selects the Segment Routing (SR) tunnel type programmed by an OSPF instance in TTM for next-hop resolution of BGP routes and labeled routes. This option allows BGP to use the segment routing tunnel in the tunnel table submitted by the lowest preference OSPF instance or, in case of a tie, the lowest numbered OSPF instance.
