## User question:
How to configure Nokia routers to allow BGP to use Segment Routing tunnels from the lowest preference OSPF instance for next-hop resolution?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure BGP to use Segment Routing tunnels from the lowest preference OSPF instance for next-hop resolution on Nokia routers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        shortcut-tunnel
            family ipv4
                resolution-filter
                    ospf
                    bgp
                    no rsvp
                    no ldp
                    no sr-isis
                    no sr-ospf
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enables BGP next-hop resolution using shortcut tunnels
2. Specifies IPv4 family (use `ipv6` if needed)
3. Configures the resolution filter to prioritize OSPF tunnels (lowest preference) followed by BGP tunnels
4. Explicitly disables other tunnel types (RSVP, LDP, SR-ISIS, SR-OSPF)

The router will now prefer OSPF tunnels first for next-hop resolution, falling back to BGP tunnels if OSPF tunnels are unavailable.
