## User question:
How to enable BGP to advertise locally configured non-local segment routing policies to BGP peers supporting the SR policy IPv4 address family on a Nokia router?
---
## Proposed answer:
To enable BGP to advertise locally configured non-local segment routing policies to BGP peers supporting the SR policy IPv4 address family on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    family sr-policy-ipv4
exit
```

If you need to configure this for a specific BGP group or neighbor, use:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    family sr-policy-ipv4
exit
```

or 

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    family sr-policy-ipv4
exit
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
sr-policy-import
no sr-policy-import
FuncDef:
This command instructs BGP to import all statically-configured non-local segment routing policies from the segment routing DB into the BGP RIB so that they can be advertised, as originated routes, towards BGP peers supporting thesr-policy-ipv4address family.
