Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To enable Segment Routing tunnel selection by TE instances for BGP next-hop resolution on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        shortcut-tunnel
            family ipv4
                resolution-filter sr-te
            exit
            family ipv6
                resolution-filter sr-te
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration enables SR-TE tunnels for both IPv4 and IPv6 BGP next-hop resolution. If you only need it for one address family, you can omit the other family block.
