## User question:
How to enable Segment Routing tunnel selection by TE instances for BGP next-hop resolution on a Nokia router?
---
## Proposed answer:
To enable Segment Routing tunnel selection by TE instances for BGP next-hop resolution on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        shortcut-tunnel
            family ipv4
                resolution-filter sr-te
            exit
            family ipv6
                resolution-filter sr-te
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration enables SR-TE tunnels for both IPv4 and IPv6 BGP next-hop resolution. If you only need it for one address family, you can omit the other family block.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
sr-te
no sr-te
FuncDef:
This command selects the Segment Routing (SR) tunnel type programmed by a traffic engineered (TE) instance in TTM for next-hop resolution. In the case of multiple SR-TE tunnels with the same lowest metric, BGP selects the tunnel with the lowest tunnel ID.
ParaDef:
No ParaDef found
