Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure TCP keepalive parameters for a station on Nokia routers, use the following BGP-related keepalive commands:

```
configure router bgp
    keepalive 30
    hold-time 90
exit
```

For more granular control at the group or neighbor level:
```
configure router bgp group "GROUP_NAME"
    keepalive 30
    hold-time 90
exit

configure router bgp group "GROUP_NAME" neighbor "IP_ADDRESS"
    keepalive 30
    hold-time 90
exit
```

Note: The values shown (keepalive=30, hold-time=90) are the defaults. Adjust these values according to your specific requirements.
