To configure the tertiary IPv4 address 192.0.2.10 for BGP optimal route reflection on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    cluster 192.0.2.10 orr-location 3
exit
```

This configures the router to use 192.0.2.10 as the cluster ID with ORR location ID 3 for optimal route reflection. The location ID range is 1-16, where 3 represents the tertiary location.
