To configure the tertiary IPv6 address 2001:db8::3 for a reference location in BGP optimal route reflection on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <peer-address>
            family ipv6
            secondary
                tertiary
                    ipv6-address 2001:db8::3
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<peer-address>` with the neighbor's IP address. This configuration adds the specified IPv6 address as a tertiary address for the BGP neighbor.
