To configure a Nokia router to preserve the original BGP next-hop when advertising routes between EBGP peers within the same IP subnet, use the following CLI command:

```
configure router bgp third-party-nexthop
```

This command ensures that when an IPv4 or IPv6 route is received from one EBGP peer and advertised to another EBGP peer in the same subnet, the BGP next-hop remains unchanged. 

If you need to apply this setting to a specific BGP group or neighbor instead of globally, use:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> third-party-nexthop
```
