Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure your Nokia router to preserve the original BGP next-hop when advertising routes between EBGP peers within the same subnet, use the following command:

```
configure router bgp third-party-nexthop
```

If you need to apply this setting to a specific BGP neighbor instead of globally, use:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <neighbor-ip> third-party-nexthop
```

These commands will ensure that when routes are advertised between EBGP peers in the same subnet, the original BGP next-hop is preserved as per RFC 4271.
