To configure tunnel resolution options for BGP labeled routes on a Nokia router, you need to enter the BGP configuration context and then access the relevant sub-contexts. Here are the CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
```

From this context, you can configure various BGP parameters including those related to labeled routes. For example, to enable backup paths for labeled IPv4 routes (which affects tunnel resolution):

```
backup-path label-ipv4
```

Or to configure best path selection criteria for labeled routes:

```
best-path-selection
as-path-ignore label-ipv4
exit
```

These commands place you in the appropriate configuration contexts for setting up tunnel resolution options for BGP labeled routes.
