Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure Nokia routers to only accept incoming BGP packets with a TTL value of at least 64, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        ttl-security 64
exit
```

Or for a specific neighbor:
```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            ttl-security 64
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the neighbor's IP address if applying to a specific peer. This ensures the router will only accept BGP packets with a TTL of 64 or higher.
