Here are the CLI commands to configure a BGP peer as an external neighbor on a Nokia router:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        type external
        peer-as <remote-as-number>
        neighbor <neighbor-ip-address>
            shutdown
            no shutdown
exit all
```

Replace:
- `<group-name>` with your BGP group name
- `<remote-as-number>` with the remote peer's AS number
- `<neighbor-ip-address>` with the IP address of the BGP neighbor

For additional common EBGP configurations, you may want to consider these optional commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        multihop <ttl-value>          # For non-directly connected EBGP peers
        remove-private                # To strip private AS numbers
        next-hop-self                 # To advertise with local BGP address as next-hop
exit all
```
