Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To enable UDP tunnel selection for BGP next-hop resolution of labeled routes on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family label-ipv4
                    resolution-filter
                        udp
                    exit
                exit
                family label-ipv6
                    resolution-filter
                        udp
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

These commands configure the router to use UDP tunnels for resolving next-hops of both IPv4 and IPv6 labeled BGP routes. You can specify either `label-ipv4` or `label-ipv6` separately if you only need one address family.
