## Proposed answer:
To enable UDP tunnel selection for BGP next-hop resolution of labeled routes on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family label-ipv4
                    resolution-filter
                        udp
                    exit
                exit
                family label-ipv6
                    resolution-filter
                        udp
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

These commands configure the router to use UDP tunnels for resolving next-hops of both IPv4 and IPv6 labeled BGP routes. You can specify either `label-ipv4` or `label-ipv6` separately if you only need one address family.
