To enable non-disruptive handling of BGP UPDATE message errors on a Nokia router when no length errors prevent NLRI field parsing, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    error-handling
exit
```

This command enables updated BGP error handling procedures at the global BGP level. The same can also be configured at the group or neighbor level if needed:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    error-handling
exit
```

or

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    error-handling
exit
```
