## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia routers to handle BGP UPDATE message errors non-disruptively when no length errors prevent NLRI field parsing, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    error-handling
exit
```

This enables updated BGP error handling procedures which help process UPDATE messages more gracefully without disrupting the session when parsing errors occur (excluding length errors).

For additional robustness, consider enabling graceful restart features:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        long-lived
            family ipv4
            family ipv6
            family vpn-ipv4
            family vpn-ipv6
        exit
    exit
    purge-timer 15
exit
```

These configurations work together to:
1. Enable improved error handling for UPDATE messages
2. Implement long-lived graceful restart for multiple address families
3. Extend the purge timer for stale routes (default is 10 minutes)
