To configure Nokia routers to apply base instance BGP export route policies to VPN-related routes including vpn-ipv4/6 and EVPN, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    vpn-apply-export
exit
```

This command ensures that the base instance BGP export route policies are applied to VPN-related routes (vpn-ipv4, vpn-ipv6, and EVPN). You can apply this at the global BGP level, group level, or neighbor level depending on your specific requirements. 

For example, if you need to apply it to a specific BGP group:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    vpn-apply-export
exit
