Generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure a Nokia router to apply base instance BGP import route policies to VPN-related routes including vpn-ipv4/6 and EVPN, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    vpn-apply-import
exit
```

This command enables the application of base instance BGP import route policies to VPN-related routes (vpn-ipv4, vpn-ipv6, and EVPN) at the global BGP level. 

If you need to apply this selectively at the group or neighbor level instead, use these variations:

For group-level configuration:
```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    vpn-apply-import
exit
```

For neighbor-level configuration:
```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    vpn-apply-import
exit
```
