To enable weighted load balancing for 6PE traffic over RSVP-TE tunnels on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    ibgp-multipath
    ebgp-ibgp-equal label-ipv6
    exit
```

These commands:
1. Enable IBGP multipath load balancing (`ibgp-multipath`)
2. Treat EBGP and IBGP routes equally for labeled IPv6 routes (`ebgp-ibgp-equal label-ipv6`), allowing for weighted load balancing across both types of paths

For proper 6PE operation, you may also need to ensure:
- Labeled IPv6 address family is enabled in your BGP configuration
- RSVP-TE tunnels are properly configured and operational
- Appropriate export policies are in place to advertise the labeled IPv6 routes
